{"ts": 1791256353.531809, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## What I built\nI built a simple assistant that operates in a file-and-calendar workspace, where it can inspect files, read notes, and send messages to help the student prepare for Friday's build.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 47, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2794765411841986, "pomdp": 0.2794765411841986, "pass_k": 0.5941893265650131}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 1.0, "motivation": 0.6197678213777771, "reliance": 0.38481971324228814, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.4205866499999997, "seen_posts": ["p3"]}}
{"ts": 1791256355.216888, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Great \u2014 the writeup is now mostly there. Last thing I\u2019d do is make the environment definition a little more explicit so it matches the instructor\u2019s wording:\n\n- **State:** files, notes, calendar events, and current messages\n- **Observations:** file contents and incoming messages\n- **Actions:** open/read files, append notes, send messages\n\nIf you want, I can polish that section too, but you\u2019re in good shape now.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=47 messages 1m", "t": 48, "activity": [{"t": 47, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2794765411841986, "pomdp": 0.2794765411841986, "pass_k": 0.5941893265650131}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 1.0, "motivation": 0.569767821377777, "reliance": 0.38481971324228814, "persistence": 0.4593844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.6944106549999995, "seen_posts": ["p3"]}}
{"ts": 1791256356.797034, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 for a POMDP, the answer is:\n\n- **POMDP = Partially Observable Markov Decision Process**\n- **State** is the true underlying situation\n- **Observations** are what the agent can actually see, which may be incomplete or noisy\n- The agent chooses **actions** based on observations, not full state\n\nIn your build context, if the environment hides some information from the agent, that\u2019s what makes it partially observable. If you want, I can help you write a one-sentence POMDP definition for your writeup too.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=48 messages 1m", "t": 49, "activity": [{"t": 48, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2794765411841986, "pomdp": 0.2880824602319257, "pass_k": 0.5941893265650131}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.75, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 1.0, "motivation": 0.569767821377777, "reliance": 0.46481971324228816, "persistence": 0.4293844359280642, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.8860874584999996, "seen_posts": ["p3"]}}
{"ts": 1791256358.237107, "type": "step", "step": 32, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the direct answer you can use:\n\n**POMDP** stands for **Partially Observable Markov Decision Process**.\n- The **state** is the true underlying situation.\n- The agent only gets **observations**, which may be incomplete or noisy.\n- The agent picks **actions** based on those observations.\n\nIf you need a one-line writeup version: *A POMDP is a decision-making model where the agent cannot directly observe the full state, only partial observations.*", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\n[activity] t=49 messages 1m", "t": 50, "activity": [{"t": 49, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2794765411841986, "pomdp": 0.2970038977064334, "pass_k": 0.5941893265650131}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.75, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 1.0, "motivation": 0.519767821377777, "reliance": 0.5448197132422882, "persistence": 0.39938443592806416, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 5.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0202612209499997, "seen_posts": ["p3"]}}
